                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Patrick</forename>
                        <surname>Patrickson</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1814-08-10"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Patrick Patrickson was a student that Godwin took an interest in and
    supported, arranging for him to attend Cambridge, with financial support from friends.  While at Cambridge 
    he was treated badly by other students and suffered from depression.  He corresponded regularly with Godwin and
    visited him when in town. Finally, when back in Cambridge, he committed suicide.  There is a single 
    Patrickson recorded in 1796 which might be Patrickson's father but this has not been coded.
  </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">P. Marshall<title>William Godwin</title>p. 286, p. 308  </bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">W. St Clair<title>The Godwins and the Shelleys</title> p. 301-2 </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
